---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/taber-and-dog.jpg';

const contacts = [
	{ label: 'GitHub', href: 'https://github.com/eltabre' },
	{ label: 'Email', href: 'mailto:taberfish@gmail.com' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
	<div class="measure">
		<div class="intro">
			<Image
				class="portrait"
				src={portrait}
				alt="Taber Fisher and his dog on a trail in the Colorado foothills"
				width={240}
				densities={[1, 2]}
				loading="eager"
			/>
			<h1>About</h1>
		</div>

		<p>
			I'm Taber Fisher, a senior AI/ML engineer in Fort Collins, Colorado. I've
			spent six years on computer vision for overhead imagery — currently
			leading a vision team at Lockheed Martin Autonomous Systems working on
			backbones and training strategies for panoptic segmentation. Before that
			I led Object-Level Change Detection, a real-time system for spotting what
			changed between two passes over the same ground, and started out on SAR
			automatic target recognition.
		</p>

		<p>
			The way I actually work is by reading widely and looking for things that
			transfer. Rendering tricks from game development turn out to be useful for
			real-time inference. That habit is also why this site is drawn as contour
			lines: a topographic map and a loss landscape are the same object — level
			sets of a function of two variables — which is a real mathematical fact
			rather than a theme I picked because it looked nice.
		</p>

		<p>
			M.S. in Machine Learning from Georgia Tech, B.S. in Computer Science from
			Virginia Tech. Three published papers, two at SPIE Defense + Commercial
			Sensing on change detection and classifier performance on low-resolution
			overhead imagery, one at GlobalSIP on EEG classifiers. Outside work it's
			mostly hiking, Blender, and Godot.
		</p>

		<ul class="contacts">
			{contacts.map((contact) => (
				<li><a href={contact.href}>{contact.label}</a></li>
			))}
		</ul>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-md);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
	}

	.intro h1 {
		margin: 0;
	}

	/* object-fit: cover crops rather than squashes; object-position pulls the
	   crop down the tall portrait so both faces land inside the circle. */
	.portrait {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 96px;
		height: 96px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: 50% 58%;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.contacts {
		list-style: none;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-md);
		margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0;
		padding-top: var(--space-md);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}
</style>
